## 1️⃣ Step 1 — Download NPPES

Get the monthly **NPPES Data Dissemination** file (Version 2) from CMS:

🔗 **`https://download.cms.gov/nppes/NPI_Files.html`**

- It's a ~1 GB zip that unzips to a ~10 GB CSV (~9.6M rows, 330 columns).
- Download the **"NPPES Data Dissemination"** file (the full monthly one, **V.2**).

**Unzip it**, then find the right file. The zip has several files — you only want the **big data file**, whose name looks like:

```
npidata_pfile_20050523-20260608.csv
```

Ignore the others:

- `..._FileHeader.csv` — just the header row (the big file already has its own header)
- `endpoint_pfile_*.csv`, `othername_pfile_*.csv`, `pl_pfile_*.csv` — extra data you don't need here

Quick way to find the one file, ignoring the header file:

```powershell
Get-ChildItem "C:\path\to\NPPES_unzipped\npidata_pfile_*.csv" |
    Where-Object { $_.Name -notlike "*FileHeader*" }
```

