## 3️⃣ Step 3 — Set up Snowflake (run once)

Creates the folder, the upload area, and the CSV-reading rules. You **don't** rebuild these on future refreshes.

```sql
-- A folder for reference/lookup tables
CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS MEDICAID.REF;

-- The holding area you'll upload files into
CREATE STAGE  IF NOT EXISTS MEDICAID.REF.NPPES_STAGE;

-- The rules for reading the CSV parts
CREATE OR REPLACE FILE FORMAT MEDICAID.REF.NPPES_CSV
  TYPE = CSV
  PARSE_HEADER = TRUE                 -- use the first row as column names
  FIELD_OPTIONALLY_ENCLOSED_BY = '"'  -- fields are wrapped in double quotes
  SKIP_BYTE_ORDER_MARK = TRUE         -- ignore the hidden BOM at the file's start
  ERROR_ON_COLUMN_COUNT_MISMATCH = FALSE;
```

**Why each line matters:**

- `PARSE_HEADER = TRUE` — lets `INFER_SCHEMA` name all 330 columns, and tells `COPY` to match by header.
- `FIELD_OPTIONALLY_ENCLOSED_BY = '"'` — NPPES wraps text in quotes (names/addresses contain commas), so fields don't split in the wrong place.
- `SKIP_BYTE_ORDER_MARK = TRUE` — the file starts with a hidden BOM. Without this, it glues onto the first column name (`NPI`) and every join on NPI silently fails.
- `ERROR_ON_COLUMN_COUNT_MISMATCH = FALSE` — a safety valve so one odd row can't abort the whole load.

