## 🔗 What's next — join to the claims data

`NPI_TAXONOMY_NAMED` attaches a specialty to each **billing** provider in the claims table. That's what lets you build peer baselines **per code × specialty × year**.

```sql
-- Attach the specialty name to each claim's billing provider
SELECT s.*,
       t.specialty_code,
       t.specialty_name
FROM MEDICAID.RAW.MEDICAID_SPENDING s
LEFT JOIN MEDICAID.REF.NPI_TAXONOMY_NAMED t
       ON s.BILLING_PROVIDER_NPI_NUM = t.npi;
```

From here you group by specialty and compare each provider to their own peer group — using the **volume** measures (`TOTAL_CLAIM_LINES`, `TOTAL_PATIENTS`) as the reliable signals.

