## 🔁 Refreshing next month

NPPES publishes a new file every month. To reload with a fresh one, empty the table and clear the old files first:

```sql
TRUNCATE TABLE MEDICAID.REF.NPPES_RAW;   -- empty the table
REMOVE @MEDICAID.REF.NPPES_STAGE;        -- clear the old staged parts
```

The schema, stage, and file format stay in place. Then repeat steps **2 → 4 → 6 → 7**, and re-run step **8c** to refresh the names.

> [!TIP]
> **Why `TRUNCATE` + `REMOVE` first?** If you skip this, `part.csv` from a test run and `part.csv.gz` from the real run count as **different files** to `COPY`, so rows get loaded twice. Clearing both guarantees a clean reload.

